IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-nouns`
IMPORT `g2-readings`
IMPORT `g2-art3-4-commissioner`

-- g2-tests-art3-4.l4: tests of Articles 3 and 4, with every expected value decided from the Law's text before the module was run.
-- A DEONTIC has no equality, so each regulative rule is exercised by a #TRACE with the outcome written above it as `-- EXPECT:`; every Boolean is asserted.

§ `Tests of Articles 3 and 4`

§§ `Article 4(1)(d): the duty to publish and maintain guidance`

GIVETH AN `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`the Commissioner publishes guidance on the operation of the Law` MEANS
    `publish and maintain guidance` `the Commissioner` `the operation of the Law, including the duties of governors and the charity test`

GIVETH AN `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`the Commissioner publishes guidance on the charity test only` MEANS
    `publish and maintain guidance` `the Commissioner` `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test`

-- src:128 | (d) to publish and maintain guidance on the operation of this Law, including guidance on the duties of governors and guidance on the charity test under Article 5(4);
-- The Commissioner publishes guidance on the operation of the Law on day 12: the duty is discharged.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 4(1)(d) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance on the operation of the Law` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `the Commissioner publishes guidance on the operation of the Law` AT 12

-- The duty names no period, so a thousand days with nothing done is not a breach: the duty stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 4(1)(d) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance on the operation of the Law` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1000)

-- Guidance on the charity test alone is guidance on one subject among those 4(1)(d) names ("including ... guidance on the charity test"): it does not discharge the duty to publish guidance on the operation of the Law.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 4(1)(d) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance on the operation of the Law` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `the Commissioner publishes guidance on the charity test only` AT 12

§§ `Article 4(2): anything calculated to facilitate a function, other than acting as a governor`

-- src:132 | (2) The Commissioner may do anything (other than acting as a governor of a charity or of an entity with charitable purposes) that is calculated to facilitate, or is conducive or incidental to, the performance of any of his or her functions.
-- Related to a function, not acting as a governor: the Commissioner has the power.
#ASSERT `Art 4(2) the Commissioner has power to do the thing` TRUE FALSE
-- Acting as a governor is excluded, however closely it relates to a function.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(2) the Commissioner has power to do the thing` TRUE TRUE
-- Not related to any function: no power, whether or not it is acting as a governor.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(2) the Commissioner has power to do the thing` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(2) the Commissioner has power to do the thing` FALSE TRUE

-- The permission is a MAY: with the power it stands until used, and using it is fulfilment; without the power there is nothing owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 4(2) the Commissioner may do the thing` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`do something that is calculated to facilitate, or is conducive or incidental to, the performance of a function` `the Commissioner`) AT 3

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 4(2) the Commissioner may do the thing` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1000)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 4(2) the Commissioner may do the thing` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1000)

§§ `Article 4(3): the three examples`

-- src:133 | (3) The Commissioner may in particular, without prejudice to the generality of his or her powers –
-- src:134 | (a) provide information to the public about the system of registration of charities, including information about the difference between charities and bodies with charitable purposes, information about the advantages of donating to entities that are registered as charities, and information by way of model constitutions;
-- src:135 | (b) advise the Minister as to the nature of charities in Jersey and as to the merits of any proposal for further regulation of charities;
-- src:136 | (c) assist a body in any jurisdiction other than Jersey, that is equivalent to the Commissioner, or to the Attorney General, the court, the Comptroller or the JFSC, in the performance of that body’s functions under the law of that jurisdiction.
-- First reading (taken): the examples illustrate 4(2).  Unrelated to a function, each is outside the power; related, each is within it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `providing information to the public about the system of registration of charities` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `advising the Minister about charities in Jersey and further regulation of them` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `assisting an equivalent body outside Jersey in the performance of its functions` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `providing information to the public about the system of registration of charities` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `advising the Minister about charities in Jersey and further regulation of them` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `assisting an equivalent body outside Jersey in the performance of its functions` TRUE FALSE
-- Acting as a governor is excluded by 4(2), and on the first reading 4(3) is bound by it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `providing information to the public about the system of registration of charities` TRUE TRUE
-- Second reading: each example is a power in its own right, so an unrelated one is within it.
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.8 read as B` `providing information to the public about the system of registration of charities` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.8 read as B` `advising the Minister about charities in Jersey and further regulation of them` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.8 read as B` `assisting an equivalent body outside Jersey in the performance of its functions` FALSE FALSE

-- The permission to assist an equivalent body abroad, where it relates to a function: it stands until used, and using it is fulfilment.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 4(3) the Commissioner may do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `assisting an equivalent body outside Jersey in the performance of its functions` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`assist an equivalent body outside Jersey in the performance of its functions` `the Commissioner`) AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 4(3) the Commissioner may do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `advising the Minister about charities in Jersey and further regulation of them` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1000)

-- Unrelated to a function, first reading: nothing is owed or permitted.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 4(3) the Commissioner may do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `advising the Minister about charities in Jersey and further regulation of them` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1000)

§§ `Article 4(4): the standard of conduct`

GIVETH A `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
`a limb that was practicable and sought` MEANS
    `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` OF TRUE, TRUE
GIVETH A `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
`a limb that was practicable and not sought` MEANS
    `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` OF TRUE, FALSE
GIVETH A `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
`a limb that was not practicable and not sought` MEANS
    `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` OF FALSE, FALSE
GIVETH A `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
`a limb that was not practicable but sought` MEANS
    `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` OF FALSE, TRUE

-- The limbs are, in order: (a) protects public trust and confidence; (a)(i) compatible with encouraging all forms of charitable giving; (a)(ii) compatible with encouraging
-- voluntary participation; (b) proportionate as to the burdens; (b) supports the development of registered charities.
GIVETH A `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
`the Commissioner sought every limb and all were practicable` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`
GIVETH A `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
`the Commissioner did not seek the last limb though all were practicable` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and not sought`
GIVETH A `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
`the Commissioner did not seek the third limb which was not practicable` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was not practicable and not sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`
GIVETH A `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
`the Commissioner did not seek the first limb which was practicable, and the last was not practicable` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF `a limb that was practicable and not sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was not practicable and not sought`
GIVETH A `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
`nothing was practicable and nothing was sought` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF `a limb that was not practicable and not sought`, `a limb that was not practicable and not sought`, `a limb that was not practicable and not sought`, `a limb that was not practicable and not sought`, `a limb that was not practicable and not sought`
GIVETH A `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
`the Commissioner sought a limb that was not practicable` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was not practicable but sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`

-- src:137 | (4) In performing his or her functions, the Commissioner must, so far appears to him or her to be reasonably practicable, seek to act in a way that –
-- src:138 | (a) protects public trust and confidence in registered charities, and is compatible with the encouragement of –
-- src:139 | (i) all forms of charitable giving, and
-- src:140 | (ii) voluntary participation in the work of registered charities; and
-- src:141 | (b) is proportionate as to the burdens imposed on, and supports the development of registered charities.
-- Every limb sought and practicable: the standard is met on either reading.
#ASSERT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `the Commissioner sought every limb and all were practicable`
#ASSERT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.9 read as B` `the Commissioner sought every limb and all were practicable`
-- A practicable limb not sought: not met on either reading.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `the Commissioner did not seek the last limb though all were practicable`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.9 read as B` `the Commissioner did not seek the last limb though all were practicable`
-- A limb that did not appear reasonably practicable need not be sought: met on either reading.
#ASSERT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `the Commissioner did not seek the third limb which was not practicable`
#ASSERT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.9 read as B` `the Commissioner did not seek the third limb which was not practicable`
-- Nothing practicable, nothing sought: met on either reading.
#ASSERT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `nothing was practicable and nothing was sought`
#ASSERT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.9 read as B` `nothing was practicable and nothing was sought`
-- Seeking a limb that was not practicable is no breach.
#ASSERT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `the Commissioner sought a limb that was not practicable`
-- Each limb in turn: practicable and not sought, with every other limb practicable and sought.  Not met, whichever limb it is.
GIVETH A `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
`only the first limb was not sought` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF `a limb that was practicable and not sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`
GIVETH A `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
`only the second limb was not sought` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and not sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`
GIVETH A `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
`only the third limb was not sought` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and not sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`
GIVETH A `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
`only the fourth limb was not sought` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`, `a limb that was practicable and not sought`, `a limb that was practicable and sought`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `only the first limb was not sought`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `only the second limb was not sought`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `only the third limb was not sought`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `only the fourth limb was not sought`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `the Commissioner did not seek the last limb though all were practicable`
-- The discriminating case of F2.9: the first limb was practicable and not sought, the last limb was not practicable.  Limb by limb, the first limb was owed and missed.  Read as a whole, it did
-- not appear reasonably practicable to act in the whole way, so the standard did not bind.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `the Commissioner did not seek the first limb which was practicable, and the last was not practicable`
#ASSERT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.9 read as B` `the Commissioner did not seek the first limb which was practicable, and the last was not practicable`

-- The duty itself: it stands until the Commissioner seeks to act in the way described.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 4(4) the Commissioner must seek to act as Article 4(4) requires` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`seek to act in a way that protects public trust and confidence in registered charities and is proportionate` `the Commissioner`) AT 2

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 4(4) the Commissioner must seek to act as Article 4(4) requires` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1000)
